EKS cluster shop: Kubernetes 1.33, status ACTIVE. Top finding: EKS cluster shop is ACTIVE with 1 health issue(s).

FINDINGS
1. [high/high] eks.cluster.unhealthy: EKS cluster shop is ACTIVE with 1 health issue(s)
   why: EKS reports control-plane problems that it cannot fix by itself, typically because a resource it depends on (subnets, security groups, the cluster IAM role, a KMS key) was changed or deleted.
   evidence (status): <<untrusted source="status">> Ec2SubnetNotFound: One or more subnets are no longer available: subnet-0dead <</untrusted>>
   fix: Fix each issue in the evidence on the AWS side (restore the subnet, security group, IAM role or KMS key permission); EKS clears the issue once the resource works again.
   docs: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/troubleshooting.html
2. [low/high] eks.cluster.public_endpoint: The API server of shop accepts connections from any IP address
   why: The endpoint is public with 0.0.0.0/0 allowed. Authentication still applies, but the API server is exposed to scanning and credential stuffing.
   evidence (spec): <<untrusted source="spec">> endpointPublicAccess=true publicAccessCidrs=0.0.0.0/0 <</untrusted>>
   fix: Restrict publicAccessCidrs to your networks, or turn the public endpoint off and use the private one.
   docs: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/cluster-endpoint.html
3. [low/high] eks.cluster.audit_logging_off: Audit logs of shop are not sent to CloudWatch
   why: Without the audit log type, who changed what in the cluster cannot be traced afterwards, and eks_logs cannot search control-plane audit events.
   evidence (spec): <<untrusted source="spec">> enabled log types: api <</untrusted>>
   fix: Enable at least the audit and authenticator log types in the cluster's logging configuration.
   docs: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/control-plane-logs.html

